statement:
Let α be a type with a σ-algebra and μ a measure on it. Let F ⊆ α be measurable with μ(F) = a for a real number a > 0. Let u : α → ℝ be measurable, with u(x) ∈ ℤ for every x and u integrable on F. Then there is an integer β such that:
(M1) |β|·a ≤ 2 ∫_F |u| dμ, stated as ofReal(|β| a) ≤ 2 ∫⁻_F ofReal|u| dμ;
(M2) β ≠ 0 implies μ(F ∩ {u ≠ 0}) ≠ 0;
(M4) ∫⁻_F ofReal|u − β| dμ ≤ ofReal(a⁻¹) ∫⁻_F ∫⁻_F ofReal|u(x) − u(y)| dμ(y) dμ(x).
